<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 01-MAY.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 01-MAY.</headline>
<text>
<p>Flood crests continue to move northward along the Red River in southern Manitoba, Canada, and should reach Winnepeg by tonight or early Friday with the worst flooding in years expected. Rivers continue to recede slowly in and around the areas of Grand Forks and Fargo, North Dakota, with slow improvement. Generally dry with just a few light showers in southern flood areas today-Saturday. The threat of heavier rainfal has diminished.</p>
</text>
